<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 04-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 04-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Andres, with 45 mph winds, is 115 miles west-southwest of Mapastepec, Mexico and moving east-northeast at 12 mph. Andres will make landfall somewhere near the southern Mexico or northern Guatemala coastline on Wednesday. Heavy rains of 5-10 inches may cause local flooding and possible mudslides as the system moves inland. Winds and rough seas may cause problems for shipping over the next 24 hours until the storm moves inland.</p>
</text>
